<title>GERMANY: German Oct wholesale prices up 0.2 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>German Oct wholesale prices up 0.2 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> GERMAN WHOLESALE PRICES	Oct 96     Sept 96	 Oct 95</p>
<p> Monthly change		    +0.2	  -0.1	   -1.4</p>
<p> Yearly change		     +0.9	  -0.7	   -0.4</p>
<p> Index (basis 1991)	     103.0	 102.8	  102.1</p>
<p>Prices for the following items rose from previous month:</p>
<p> Sea fish					+25.0  pct</p>
<p> Heating oil				   +13.0  pct</p>
<p> Oranges					 +12.0  pct</p>
<p> Diesel fuel				    +6.8  pct</p>
<p> Eggs					     +3.8  pct</p>
<p> Raw coffee				     +2.5  pct</p>
<p> Cigarettes				     +1.3  pct</p>
<p> Gasoline					 +0.9  pct</p>
<p>The following items fell from the previous month:</p>
<p> Refrigerated meat			    -7.5  pct</p>
<p> Live pigs					-6.8  pct</p>
<p> Fresh non-citrus fruit		     -6.0  pct</p>
<p> Bananas					  -5.6  pct</p>
<p> Fresh vegetables			     -5.2  pct</p>
<p> Grain					    -1.3  pct</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
